{"title":"1969 AHSME Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let a binary operation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d17950ad2ab63c764778b133f95a03dcf2969d57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\star$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> on ordered pairs of integers be defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f4562a61586be5fd2a12781662dda7ab6b5d85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)\\star (c,d)=(a-c,b+d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />. Then, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b78901e3650a5ceb63ea4ea974ed4fefcaa10d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,3)\\star (0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/297637ec08c8007bd5ec1deeb216508bfc2e12b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)\\star (3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" /> represent identical pairs, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> equals:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/205abcb4c11d77fffbb4782714d3d5f1cd49fe53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } -3\\quad \\text{(B) } 0\\quad \\text{(C) } 2\\quad \\text{(D) } 3\\quad \\text{(E) } 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"286\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Performing the operation based on the definition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/d/85d69322d0358df5b6cbc9c035fd55a429692b32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,3)\\star(0,0) = (3,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f117662c291fd1379a0c13da34edbf9356581f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)\\star(3,2)=(x-3,y+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"227\" height=\"18\" />.  Because the outputs are identical pairs, they must equal each other, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/3/113b664d3ec1abd335927b46b5554481d7377009.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 = x-3$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />.  Solving for x yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea7da1b75cc1a945018db7316c26d618ca11ff9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, which is answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_AHSME\" title=\"1969 AHSME\">1969 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?ti